@lang en

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `uk-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `uk-interpretation-application`
IMPORT `uk-interpretation-schedule1`

-- The Interpretation Act 1978 (1978 c. 30): the entries of Schedule 1 whose meaning is more than a pointer, and the paragraphs of
-- Schedule 2 that change a definition for an earlier Act (paras 4(2), 4(3), 4(5), 4(6) and 5).
--
-- Source: the converter-made plain-text rendering in ../../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-1978-30.txt, not the official text (see SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
--
-- uk-interpretation-schedule1.l4 holds every entry as the Act states it. This module holds what an entry DECIDES: whether a place is in the
-- British Islands, whether a territory is a colony, whether a thing is land, whether a body is a person, and the like. A boolean named
-- "Schedule 1 counts ... as ..." answers TRUE when the entry says so and FALSE when the entry does not say so; FALSE never means that the
-- opposite is the law, because most entries "include" and so do not shut anything out.
-- Whether an entry reaches a given enactment at all (its bracket, Sch 2 para 4(1)) is answered in uk-interpretation-schedule1.l4.
--
-- A borrowed fact (the day the Irish Free State was established, the day the Welsh Language Act 1967 was passed, the limit that section 224(1) of the
-- Sentencing Code lays down) is asked as an input. Where the text does not choose, the function refuses by name and the tests assert the refusal.

§ `Named refusals of this module`

-- A refusal is an expression at any type; each name is its message.
-- Sch 2 paras 4(2), 4(3)(b) and 5(a) refuse on the very day of the event they compare with (fork F22); para 4(3)(a) reads an Act passed on the day the exclusion
-- operated as passed with the exclusion in force (fork F23); para 4(6) refuses where the mark of a Schedule 1 paragraph could go either way (fork F24).

-- src:416 | (2) The definition of “British Islands”, in its application to Acts passed after the establishment of the Irish Free State but before the commencement of this Act, includes the Republic of Ireland.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 2 para 4(2) (src:416): "after the establishment of the Irish Free State": an Act passed on the very day does not say whether it was passed after it
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Schedule 2 para 4(2) does not say whether an Act passed on the day the Irish Free State was established was passed after it` MEANS
    REFUSE "Schedule 2 para 4(2) does not say whether an Act passed on the day the Irish Free State was established was passed after it"

-- src:343 | In relation to a term of imprisonment in respect of an offence triable either way under the law of England and Wales, “general limit in a magistrates’ court” means the limit laid down in respect of the offence by section 224(1) of the Sentencing Code (as it has effect from time to time).
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 1, offences paragraph (src:343): "In relation to a term of imprisonment in respect of an offence triable either way under the law of England and Wales"
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Schedule 1 gives no general limit in a magistrates' court for an offence that is not triable either way under the law of England and Wales` MEANS
    REFUSE "Schedule 1 gives no general limit in a magistrates' court for an offence that is not triable either way under the law of England and Wales"

@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 1, offences paragraph (src:343): the limit is that laid down by section 224(1) of the Sentencing Code, which is not among the sources
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Schedule 1 points at section 224(1) of the Sentencing Code for the general limit, and the sources do not give it, so the caller must say what it is` MEANS
    REFUSE "Schedule 1 points at section 224(1) of the Sentencing Code for the general limit, and the sources do not give it, so the caller must say what it is"

-- src:417 | (3) The definition of “colony”, in its application to an Act passed at any time before the commencement of this Act, includes—
-- src:419 | (b) any country or territory which ceased after that time to be part of Her Majesty’s dominions but subject to a provision for the continuation of existing law as if it had not so ceased;
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 2 para 4(3)(b) (src:417) and (src:419): "ceased after that time": an event on the day the Act was passed does not say whether it came after
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Schedule 2 para 4(3)(b) does not say whether a territory that ceased on the day the Act was passed ceased after it` MEANS
    REFUSE "Schedule 2 para 4(3)(b) does not say whether a territory that ceased on the day the Act was passed ceased after it"

-- src:423 | (6) This paragraph applies to . . . the Water Act 1973 as if they were passed after 1st April 1974.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 2 para 4(6) (src:423): "as if they were passed after 1st April 1974" names no day
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Schedule 2 para 4(6) treats the Act as passed after 1st April 1974 and names no day, so the mark of the paragraph is not decided` MEANS
    REFUSE "Schedule 2 para 4(6) treats the Act as passed after 1st April 1974 and names no day, so the mark of the paragraph is not decided"

-- src:424 | 5 The following definitions shall be treated as included in Schedule 1 for the purposes specified in this paragraph—
-- src:425 | (a) in any Act passed before 1st April 1974, a reference to England includes Berwick upon Tweed and Monmouthshire and, in the case of an Act passed before the Welsh Language Act 1967, Wales;
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 2 para 5(a) (src:424-425): "in the case of an Act passed before the Welsh Language Act 1967, Wales": an Act passed on the very day does not say whether it was passed before it
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Schedule 2 para 5(a) does not say whether an Act passed on the day the Welsh Language Act 1967 was passed was passed before it` MEANS
    REFUSE "Schedule 2 para 5(a) does not say whether an Act passed on the day the Welsh Language Act 1967 was passed was passed before it"

§ `Schedule 1 "British Islands" and Schedule 2 para 4(2)`

DECLARE `A place` IS ONE OF
    `the United Kingdom`
    `the Channel Islands`
    `the Isle of Man`
    `the Republic of Ireland`
    `another place`

-- src:229 | “British Islands” means the United Kingdom, the Channel Islands and the Isle of Man. [1889]
-- src:416 | (2) The definition of “British Islands”, in its application to Acts passed after the establishment of the Irish Free State but before the commencement of this Act, includes the Republic of Ireland.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 1 "British Islands" (src:229); Sch 2 para 4(2) (src:416)
GIVEN place IS A `A place`
      day IS A DATE
      `the day the Irish Free State was established` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 counts the place as part of the British Islands for an Act passed on` place day `the day the Irish Free State was established` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `the United Kingdom` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Channel Islands` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Isle of Man` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Republic of Ireland` THEN
        BRANCH
            IF day AT LEAST `the day on which the Interpretation Act 1978 comes into force` THEN FALSE
            IF day GREATER THAN `the day the Irish Free State was established` THEN TRUE
            IF day EQUALS `the day the Irish Free State was established`
                THEN `Schedule 2 para 4(2) does not say whether an Act passed on the day the Irish Free State was established was passed after it`
            OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHEN `another place` THEN FALSE

§ `Schedule 1 "British possession", "Colony", "Colonial legislature" and "Governor-General"`

-- src:231 | “British possession” means any part of Her Majesty’s dominions outside the United Kingdom; and where parts of such dominions are under both a central and a local legislature, all parts under the central legislature are deemed, for the purposes of this definition, to be one British possession. [1889]
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 1 "British possession" (src:231): "any part of Her Majesty's dominions outside the United Kingdom"
GIVEN `it is a part of Her Majesty's dominions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 counts the territory as a British possession` `it is a part of Her Majesty's dominions` `it is outside the United Kingdom` MEANS
        `it is a part of Her Majesty's dominions`
    AND `it is outside the United Kingdom`

-- "where parts of such dominions are under both a central and a local legislature, all parts under the central legislature are deemed, for the purposes of this
-- definition, to be one British possession": the deeming applies to the parts under the central legislature, and to no others.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 1 "British possession" (src:231): the deeming of parts under a central legislature
GIVEN `parts of the dominions are under both a central and a local legislature` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this part is under the central legislature` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 treats the parts under a central legislature as one British possession` `parts of the dominions are under both a central and a local legislature` `this part is under the central legislature` MEANS
        `parts of the dominions are under both a central and a local legislature`
    AND `this part is under the central legislature`

-- src:238 | “Colonial legislature”, and “legislature” in relation to a British possession, mean the authority, other than the Parliament of the United Kingdom or Her Majesty in Council, competent to make laws for the possession. [1889]
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 1 "Colonial legislature" and "legislature" (src:238)
GIVEN `it is an authority competent to make laws for the possession` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the Parliament of the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is Her Majesty in Council` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 counts the authority as a colonial legislature` `it is an authority competent to make laws for the possession` `it is the Parliament of the United Kingdom` `it is Her Majesty in Council` MEANS
        `it is an authority competent to make laws for the possession`
    AND NOT `it is the Parliament of the United Kingdom`
    AND NOT `it is Her Majesty in Council`

-- src:239 | “Colony” means any part of Her Majesty’s dominions outside the British Islands except—
-- src:240 | (a) countries having fully responsible status within the Commonwealth;
-- src:241 | (b) territories for whose external relations a country other than the United Kingdom is responsible;
-- src:242 | (c) associated states:
-- src:243 | and where parts of such dominions are under both a central and a local legislature, all parts under the central legislature are deemed for the purposes of this definition to be one colony. [1889]
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 1 "Colony" (src:239-243)
GIVEN `it is a part of Her Majesty's dominions outside the British Islands` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a country having fully responsible status within the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a territory for whose external relations a country other than the United Kingdom is responsible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an associated state` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 counts the territory as a colony` `it is a part of Her Majesty's dominions outside the British Islands` `it is a country having fully responsible status within the Commonwealth` `it is a territory for whose external relations a country other than the United Kingdom is responsible` `it is an associated state` MEANS
        `it is a part of Her Majesty's dominions outside the British Islands`
    AND NOT `it is a country having fully responsible status within the Commonwealth`
    AND NOT `it is a territory for whose external relations a country other than the United Kingdom is responsible`
    AND NOT `it is an associated state`

@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 1 "Colony" (src:239-243): "all parts under the central legislature are deemed for the purposes of this definition to be one colony"
GIVEN `parts of the dominions are under both a central and a local legislature` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this part is under the central legislature` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 treats the parts under a central legislature as one colony` `parts of the dominions are under both a central and a local legislature` `this part is under the central legislature` MEANS
        `parts of the dominions are under both a central and a local legislature`
    AND `this part is under the central legislature`

DECLARE `Governor term` IS ONE OF
    `Governor-General`
    `Governor, in relation to a British possession`

-- src:269 | “Governor-General” includes any person who for the time being has the powers of the Governor-General, and “Governor”, in relation to any British possession, includes the officer for the time being administering the government of that possession. [1889]
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 1 "Governor-General" and "Governor" (src:269)
GIVEN term IS A `Governor term`
      `the person for the time being has the powers of the Governor-General` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the officer for the time being administering the government of the possession` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 counts the person as a Governor-General or Governor` term `the person for the time being has the powers of the Governor-General` `the person is the officer for the time being administering the government of the possession` MEANS
    CONSIDER term
    WHEN `Governor-General` THEN `the person for the time being has the powers of the Governor-General`
    WHEN `Governor, in relation to a British possession` THEN `the person is the officer for the time being administering the government of the possession`

§ `Schedule 2 para 4(3): "colony" for an Act passed before the commencement`

-- "(3) The definition of colony, in its application to an Act passed at any time before the commencement of this Act, includes (a) any colony within the meaning of
-- section 18(3) of the Interpretation Act 1889 which was excluded, but in relation only to Acts passed at a later time, by any enactment repealed by this Act;
-- (b) any country or territory which ceased after that time to be part of Her Majesty's dominions but subject to a provision for the continuation of existing law as if it
-- had not so ceased; and paragraph (b) of the definition does not apply."
-- "That time" and "a later time" are the time at which the Act was passed. The section 18(3) of the 1889 Act and the repealing enactments are not among the sources.
-- src:417 | (3) The definition of “colony”, in its application to an Act passed at any time before the commencement of this Act, includes—
-- src:418 | (a) any colony within the meaning of section 18(3) of the Interpretation Act 1889 which was excluded, but in relation only to Acts passed at a later time, by any enactment repealed by this Act;
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 2 para 4(3)(a) (src:417-418): "excluded, but in relation only to Acts passed at a later time"
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the day from which an enactment repealed by this Act excluded it` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 2 para 4(3)(a) provides that the Act was passed before the exclusion took effect` day `the day from which an enactment repealed by this Act excluded it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day from which an enactment repealed by this Act excluded it`
    WHEN JUST excluded THEN day LESS THAN excluded
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

-- src:417 | (3) The definition of “colony”, in its application to an Act passed at any time before the commencement of this Act, includes—
-- src:419 | (b) any country or territory which ceased after that time to be part of Her Majesty’s dominions but subject to a provision for the continuation of existing law as if it had not so ceased;
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 2 para 4(3)(b) (src:417) and (src:419): "ceased after that time to be part of Her Majesty's dominions"
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the day it ceased to be part of Her Majesty's dominions` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 2 para 4(3)(b) provides that the territory ceased after the Act was passed to be part of Her Majesty's dominions` day `the day it ceased to be part of Her Majesty's dominions` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day it ceased to be part of Her Majesty's dominions`
    WHEN JUST ceased THEN
        BRANCH
            IF ceased GREATER THAN day THEN TRUE
            IF ceased EQUALS day THEN `Schedule 2 para 4(3)(b) does not say whether a territory that ceased on the day the Act was passed ceased after it`
            OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

-- src:417 | (3) The definition of “colony”, in its application to an Act passed at any time before the commencement of this Act, includes—
-- src:418 | (a) any colony within the meaning of section 18(3) of the Interpretation Act 1889 which was excluded, but in relation only to Acts passed at a later time, by any enactment repealed by this Act;
-- src:419 | (b) any country or territory which ceased after that time to be part of Her Majesty’s dominions but subject to a provision for the continuation of existing law as if it had not so ceased;
-- src:420 | and paragraph (b) of the definition does not apply.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 2 para 4(3) (src:417-420), read with Sch 1 "Colony" (src:239-243)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `it is a part of Her Majesty's dominions outside the British Islands` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a country having fully responsible status within the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a territory for whose external relations a country other than the United Kingdom is responsible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an associated state` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a colony within the meaning of section 18(3) of the Interpretation Act 1889` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day from which an enactment repealed by this Act excluded it` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day it ceased to be part of Her Majesty's dominions` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `a provision continues the existing law as if it had not ceased` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 2 para 4(3) counts the territory as a colony for an Act passed on` day `it is a part of Her Majesty's dominions outside the British Islands` `it is a country having fully responsible status within the Commonwealth` `it is a territory for whose external relations a country other than the United Kingdom is responsible` `it is an associated state` `it is a colony within the meaning of section 18(3) of the Interpretation Act 1889` `the day from which an enactment repealed by this Act excluded it` `the day it ceased to be part of Her Majesty's dominions` `a provision continues the existing law as if it had not ceased` MEANS
    IF   `the day is on or after the commencement of the Interpretation Act 1978` day
    THEN `Schedule 1 counts the territory as a colony` `it is a part of Her Majesty's dominions outside the British Islands` `it is a country having fully responsible status within the Commonwealth` `it is a territory for whose external relations a country other than the United Kingdom is responsible` `it is an associated state`
    ELSE    (`it is a part of Her Majesty's dominions outside the British Islands` AND (NOT `it is a country having fully responsible status within the Commonwealth`) AND (NOT `it is an associated state`))
         OR (`it is a colony within the meaning of section 18(3) of the Interpretation Act 1889` AND `Schedule 2 para 4(3)(a) provides that the Act was passed before the exclusion took effect` day `the day from which an enactment repealed by this Act excluded it`)
         OR (`a provision continues the existing law as if it had not ceased` AND `Schedule 2 para 4(3)(b) provides that the territory ceased after the Act was passed to be part of Her Majesty's dominions` day `the day it ceased to be part of Her Majesty's dominions`)

§ `Schedule 1 "Enactment", "Land", "Oath", "Person", "Writing" and "Rules of Court"`

-- src:266 | “Enactment” includes any assimilated direct legislation but does not include an enactment comprised in, or in an instrument made under, an Act of the Scottish Parliament.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 1 "Enactment" (src:266)
GIVEN `it is an enactment apart from this entry` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is assimilated direct legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is comprised in, or in an instrument made under, an Act of the Scottish Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 counts the legislation as an enactment` `it is an enactment apart from this entry` `it is assimilated direct legislation` `it is comprised in, or in an instrument made under, an Act of the Scottish Parliament` MEANS
        NOT `it is comprised in, or in an instrument made under, an Act of the Scottish Parliament`
    AND (`it is an enactment apart from this entry` OR `it is assimilated direct legislation`)

DECLARE `Thing that may be land` IS ONE OF
    `a building`
    `another structure`
    `land covered with water`
    `an estate in or over land`
    `an interest in or over land`
    `an easement in or over land`
    `a servitude in or over land`
    `a right in or over land`
    `a messuage`
    `a tenement or hereditament`
    `a house or building of any tenure`
    `something else`

-- src:276 | “Land” includes building and other structures, land covered with water, and any estate, interest, easement, servitude or right in or over land. [1st January 1979].
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 1 "Land" (src:276)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing that may be land`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 counts the thing as land` thing MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `a building` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `another structure` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `land covered with water` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an estate in or over land` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an interest in or over land` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an easement in or over land` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a servitude in or over land` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a right in or over land` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a messuage` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a tenement or hereditament` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a house or building of any tenure` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `something else` THEN FALSE

DECLARE `Word of the entry on oaths` IS ONE OF
    `oath`
    `affidavit`
    `swear`

DECLARE `Word the entry includes` IS ONE OF
    `affirmation`
    `declaration`
    `affirm`
    `declare`
    `another word`

-- src:291 | “Oath” and “affidavit” include affirmation and declaration, and “swear” includes affirm and declare.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 1 "Oath", "affidavit" and "swear" (src:291)
GIVEN word IS A `Word of the entry on oaths`
      included IS A `Word the entry includes`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 counts the word as included in oath, affidavit or swear` word included MEANS
    CONSIDER word
    WHEN `oath` THEN included EQUALS `affirmation` OR included EQUALS `declaration`
    WHEN `affidavit` THEN included EQUALS `affirmation` OR included EQUALS `declaration`
    WHEN `swear` THEN included EQUALS `affirm` OR included EQUALS `declare`

-- src:298 | “Person” includes a body of persons corporate or unincorporate. [1889]
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 1 "Person" (src:298)
GIVEN `it is a body of persons corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a body of persons unincorporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 counts the body as a person` `it is a body of persons corporate` `it is a body of persons unincorporate` MEANS
    `it is a body of persons corporate` OR `it is a body of persons unincorporate`

DECLARE `Mode of representing words` IS ONE OF
    `typing`
    `printing`
    `lithography`
    `photography`
    `another mode of representing or reproducing words in a visible form`
    `a mode that does not represent or reproduce words in a visible form`

-- src:333 | “Writing” includes typing, printing, lithography, photography and other modes of representing or reproducing words in a visible form, and expressions referring to writing are construed accordingly.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 1 "Writing" (src:333)
GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of representing words`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 counts the mode of representing words as writing` mode MEANS
    CONSIDER mode
    WHEN `typing` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `printing` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `lithography` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `photography` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `another mode of representing or reproducing words in a visible form` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a mode that does not represent or reproduce words in a visible form` THEN FALSE

-- "and expressions referring to writing are construed accordingly".
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 1 "Writing" (src:333): "expressions referring to writing are construed accordingly"
GIVEN `the expression refers to writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the mode it refers to is writing under the entry` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 construes the expression referring to writing accordingly` `the expression refers to writing` `the mode it refers to is writing under the entry` MEANS
    `the expression refers to writing` AND `the mode it refers to is writing under the entry`

-- src:310 | “Rules of Court” in relation to any court means rules made by the authority having power to make rules or orders regulating the practice and procedure of that court, and in Scotland includes Acts of Adjournal and Acts of Sederunt; and the power of the authority to make rules of court (as above defined) includes power to make such rules for the purpose of any Act which directs or authorises anything to be done by rules of court. [1889]
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 1 "Rules of Court" (src:310): "rules made by the authority having power to make rules or orders regulating the practice and procedure of that court, and in Scotland includes Acts of Adjournal and Acts of Sederunt"
GIVEN `it is made by the authority having power to make rules or orders regulating the practice and procedure of that court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an Act of Adjournal or an Act of Sederunt` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 counts the instrument as Rules of Court` `it is made by the authority having power to make rules or orders regulating the practice and procedure of that court` `it is an Act of Adjournal or an Act of Sederunt` `it is in Scotland` MEANS
        `it is made by the authority having power to make rules or orders regulating the practice and procedure of that court`
    OR (`it is an Act of Adjournal or an Act of Sederunt` AND `it is in Scotland`)

@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 1 "Rules of Court" (src:310): "the power of the authority to make rules of court (as above defined) includes power to make such rules for the purpose of any Act which directs or authorises anything to be done by rules of court"
GIVEN `it is the power of the authority to make rules of court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rules are for the purpose of an Act which directs or authorises anything to be done by rules of court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 includes in the power to make Rules of Court the power to make them for the purpose of an Act` `it is the power of the authority to make rules of court` `the rules are for the purpose of an Act which directs or authorises anything to be done by rules of court` MEANS
    `it is the power of the authority to make rules of court` AND `the rules are for the purpose of an Act which directs or authorises anything to be done by rules of court`

§ `Schedule 1 "Bank of England", "Bank of Ireland" and "Parliamentary Election"`

DECLARE `Bank named in Schedule 1` IS ONE OF
    `Bank of England`
    `Bank of Ireland`

-- src:227 | “Bank of England” means, as the context requires, the Governor and Company of the Bank of England or the bank of the Governor and Company of the Bank of England.
-- src:228 | “Bank of Ireland” means, as the context requires, the Governor and Company of the Bank of Ireland or the bank of the Governor and Company of the Bank of Ireland.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 1 "Bank of England" (src:227) and "Bank of Ireland" (src:228)
GIVEN bank IS A `Bank named in Schedule 1`
      `the context requires the bank of the Governor and Company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A STRING
`Schedule 1 — what Bank of England and Bank of Ireland mean as the context requires` bank `the context requires the bank of the Governor and Company` MEANS
    CONSIDER bank
    WHEN `Bank of England` THEN
        IF   `the context requires the bank of the Governor and Company`
        THEN "the bank of the Governor and Company of the Bank of England"
        ELSE "the Governor and Company of the Bank of England"
    WHEN `Bank of Ireland` THEN
        IF   `the context requires the bank of the Governor and Company`
        THEN "the bank of the Governor and Company of the Bank of Ireland"
        ELSE "the Governor and Company of the Bank of Ireland"

-- src:295 | “Parliamentary Election” means the election of a Member to serve in Parliament for a constituency. [1889]
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 1 "Parliamentary Election" (src:295)
GIVEN `it is an election of a Member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Member is to serve in Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Member is to serve for a constituency` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 counts the election as a Parliamentary election` `it is an election of a Member` `the Member is to serve in Parliament` `the Member is to serve for a constituency` MEANS
        `it is an election of a Member`
    AND `the Member is to serve in Parliament`
    AND `the Member is to serve for a constituency`

§ `Schedule 1 "The Income Tax Acts", "The Corporation Tax Acts" and "The Tax Acts"`

-- src:251 | “The Corporation Tax Acts” means the enactments relating to the taxation of the income and chargeable gains of companies and of company distributions (including provisions relating to income tax);
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 1 "The Corporation Tax Acts" (src:251)
GIVEN `it relates to the taxation of the income and chargeable gains of companies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it relates to the taxation of company distributions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a provision relating to income tax within such an enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 counts the enactment among the Corporation Tax Acts` `it relates to the taxation of the income and chargeable gains of companies` `it relates to the taxation of company distributions` `it is a provision relating to income tax within such an enactment` MEANS
        `it relates to the taxation of the income and chargeable gains of companies`
    OR  `it relates to the taxation of company distributions`
    OR  `it is a provision relating to income tax within such an enactment`

-- src:275 | “The Income Tax Acts” means all enactments relating to income tax, including any provisions of the Corporation Tax Acts which relate to income tax.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 1 "The Income Tax Acts" (src:275)
GIVEN `it relates to income tax` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 counts the enactment among the Income Tax Acts` `it relates to income tax` MEANS
    `it relates to income tax`

-- src:327 | “The Tax Acts” means the Income Tax Acts and the Corporation Tax Acts.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 1 "The Tax Acts" (src:327)
GIVEN `it is among the Income Tax Acts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is among the Corporation Tax Acts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 counts the enactment among the Tax Acts` `it is among the Income Tax Acts` `it is among the Corporation Tax Acts` MEANS
    `it is among the Income Tax Acts` OR `it is among the Corporation Tax Acts`

§ `Schedule 1: the entries about the European Union`

-- src:366 | “EEA state”, in relation to a time, means—
-- src:367 | (a) a state which at that time is a member State, or
-- src:368 | (b) any other state which at that time is a party to the EEA agreement. [8 January 2007]
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 1 "EEA state" (src:366-368)
GIVEN `it is a member State at that time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a party to the EEA agreement at that time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 counts the state as an EEA state at the time` `it is a member State at that time` `it is a party to the EEA agreement at that time` MEANS
    `it is a member State at that time` OR `it is a party to the EEA agreement at that time`

-- src:373 | “EU instrument” means any instrument issued by an EU institution other than any assimilated direct legislation.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 1 "EU instrument" (src:373)
GIVEN `it is an instrument issued by an EU institution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is assimilated direct legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 counts the instrument as an EU instrument` `it is an instrument issued by an EU institution` `it is assimilated direct legislation` MEANS
    `it is an instrument issued by an EU institution` AND NOT `it is assimilated direct legislation`

DECLARE `Instrument asked about under the EEA agreement entry` IS ONE OF
    `the agreement on the European Economic Area signed at Oporto on 2 May 1992`
    `the Protocol adjusting that Agreement signed at Brussels on 17 March 1993`
    `a modification or supplement of either, as made from time to time`
    `assimilated direct legislation`
    `something else`

-- src:365 | “EEA agreement” means the agreement on the European Economic Area signed at Oporto on 2 May 1992, together with the Protocol adjusting that Agreement signed at Brussels on 17 March 1993, as modified or supplemented from time to time, but does not include any assimilated direct legislation. [8 January 2007]
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 1 "EEA agreement" (src:365)
GIVEN thing IS AN `Instrument asked about under the EEA agreement entry`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 includes the thing in the EEA agreement` thing MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `the agreement on the European Economic Area signed at Oporto on 2 May 1992` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Protocol adjusting that Agreement signed at Brussels on 17 March 1993` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a modification or supplement of either, as made from time to time` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `assimilated direct legislation` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `something else` THEN FALSE

-- src:363 | “The Communities” means Euratom, the Economic Community and the Coal and Steel Community, but a reference to any or all of those Communities is to be treated as being or including (as the context requires) a reference to the EU.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 1 "The Communities" (src:363): "a reference to any or all of those Communities is to be treated as being or including (as the context requires) a reference to the EU"
GIVEN `the context requires a reference to the EU` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 treats a reference to a Community as including the EU` `the context requires a reference to the EU` MEANS
    `the context requires a reference to the EU`

-- src:371 | “The EU” or “the European Union” means the European Union, being the Union established by the Treaty on European Union signed at Maastricht on 7 February 1992 (as amended by any later Treaty); and includes, so far as the context permits or requires, Euratom.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 1 "The EU" or "the European Union" (src:371): "includes, so far as the context permits or requires, Euratom"
GIVEN `the context permits it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the context requires it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 includes Euratom in the EU where the context permits or requires` `the context permits it` `the context requires it` MEANS
    `the context permits it` OR `the context requires it`

-- src:359 | “Assimilated obligation” means an obligation that—
-- src:360 | (a) was created or arose by or under the EU Treaties before IP completion day, and
-- src:361 | (b) forms part of assimilated law,
-- src:362 | as modified from time to time.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 1 "Assimilated obligation" (src:359-362)
GIVEN `it was created or arose by or under the EU Treaties before IP completion day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it forms part of assimilated law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 counts the obligation as an assimilated obligation` `it was created or arose by or under the EU Treaties before IP completion day` `it forms part of assimilated law` MEANS
    `it was created or arose by or under the EU Treaties before IP completion day` AND `it forms part of assimilated law`

§ `Schedule 1: construction of certain expressions relating to offences`

DECLARE `Way an offence is triable if committed by an adult` IS ONE OF
    `triable on indictment only`
    `triable either on indictment or summarily`
    `triable only summarily`

DECLARE `Term of the paragraph on offences` IS ONE OF
    `indictable offence`
    `summary offence`
    `offence triable either way`
    `indictable`
    `summary`
    `triable either way`

-- src:336 | Construction of certain expressions relating to offences
-- src:337 | In relation to England and Wales—
-- src:338 | (a) “indictable offence” means an offence which, if committed by an adult, is triable on indictment, whether it is exclusively so triable or triable either way;
-- src:339 | (b) “summary offence” means an offence which, if committed by an adult, is triable only summarily;
-- src:340 | (c) “offence triable either way” means an offence , other than an offence triable on indictment only by virtue of Part V of the Criminal Justice Act 1988 which, if committed by an adult, is triable either on indictment or summarily;
-- src:341 | and the terms “indictable”, “summary” and “triable either way”, in their application to offences, are to be construed accordingly.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 1, offences paragraph (src:336-341)
GIVEN term IS A `Term of the paragraph on offences`
      way IS A `Way an offence is triable if committed by an adult`
      `it is triable on indictment only by virtue of Part V of the Criminal Justice Act 1988` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 construes the term as applied to an offence triable in England and Wales` term way `it is triable on indictment only by virtue of Part V of the Criminal Justice Act 1988` MEANS
    CONSIDER term
    WHEN `indictable offence` THEN way EQUALS `triable on indictment only` OR way EQUALS `triable either on indictment or summarily`
    WHEN `summary offence` THEN way EQUALS `triable only summarily`
    WHEN `offence triable either way` THEN way EQUALS `triable either on indictment or summarily` AND NOT `it is triable on indictment only by virtue of Part V of the Criminal Justice Act 1988`
    WHEN `indictable` THEN way EQUALS `triable on indictment only` OR way EQUALS `triable either on indictment or summarily`
    WHEN `summary` THEN way EQUALS `triable only summarily`
    WHEN `triable either way` THEN way EQUALS `triable either on indictment or summarily` AND NOT `it is triable on indictment only by virtue of Part V of the Criminal Justice Act 1988`

-- (a), (b) and (c) are each their own function so that each limb has its own place; they apply the dispatcher to their own term.
-- src:338 | (a) “indictable offence” means an offence which, if committed by an adult, is triable on indictment, whether it is exclusively so triable or triable either way;
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 1, offences paragraph (a) (src:338)
GIVEN way IS A `Way an offence is triable if committed by an adult`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 counts the offence as an indictable offence` way MEANS
    `Schedule 1 construes the term as applied to an offence triable in England and Wales` `indictable offence` way FALSE

-- src:339 | (b) “summary offence” means an offence which, if committed by an adult, is triable only summarily;
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 1, offences paragraph (b) (src:339)
GIVEN way IS A `Way an offence is triable if committed by an adult`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 counts the offence as a summary offence` way MEANS
    `Schedule 1 construes the term as applied to an offence triable in England and Wales` `summary offence` way FALSE

-- src:340 | (c) “offence triable either way” means an offence , other than an offence triable on indictment only by virtue of Part V of the Criminal Justice Act 1988 which, if committed by an adult, is triable either on indictment or summarily;
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 1, offences paragraph (c) (src:340)
GIVEN way IS A `Way an offence is triable if committed by an adult`
      `it is triable on indictment only by virtue of Part V of the Criminal Justice Act 1988` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 counts the offence as an offence triable either way` way `it is triable on indictment only by virtue of Part V of the Criminal Justice Act 1988` MEANS
    `Schedule 1 construes the term as applied to an offence triable in England and Wales` `offence triable either way` way `it is triable on indictment only by virtue of Part V of the Criminal Justice Act 1988`

-- "references to the way or ways in which an offence is triable are to be construed without regard to the effect, if any, of section 22 of the Magistrates' Courts Act 1980
-- on the mode of trial in a particular case": the way an offence is triable in general is the way, whatever section 22 does in the particular case.
-- src:342 | In the above definitions references to the way or ways in which an offence is triable are to be construed without regard to the effect, if any, of section 22 of the Magistrates’ Courts Act 1980 on the mode of trial in a particular case.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 1, offences paragraph (src:342)
GIVEN `the way the offence is triable in general` IS A `Way an offence is triable if committed by an adult`
      `the way it is tried in the particular case after section 22 of the Magistrates' Courts Act 1980` IS A `Way an offence is triable if committed by an adult`
GIVETH A `Way an offence is triable if committed by an adult`
`Schedule 1 reads the way an offence is triable without regard to section 22 of the Magistrates' Courts Act 1980` `the way the offence is triable in general` `the way it is tried in the particular case after section 22 of the Magistrates' Courts Act 1980` MEANS
    `the way the offence is triable in general`

-- src:343 | In relation to a term of imprisonment in respect of an offence triable either way under the law of England and Wales, “general limit in a magistrates’ court” means the limit laid down in respect of the offence by section 224(1) of the Sentencing Code (as it has effect from time to time).
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 1, offences paragraph (src:343)
GIVEN `the offence is triable either way under the law of England and Wales` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the limit laid down in respect of the offence by section 224(1) of the Sentencing Code as it has effect from time to time` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Schedule 1 — the general limit in a magistrates' court` `the offence is triable either way under the law of England and Wales` `the limit laid down in respect of the offence by section 224(1) of the Sentencing Code as it has effect from time to time` MEANS
    IF   NOT `the offence is triable either way under the law of England and Wales`
    THEN `Schedule 1 gives no general limit in a magistrates' court for an offence that is not triable either way under the law of England and Wales`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the limit laid down in respect of the offence by section 224(1) of the Sentencing Code as it has effect from time to time`
         WHEN JUST n THEN n
         WHEN NOTHING THEN `Schedule 1 points at section 224(1) of the Sentencing Code for the general limit, and the sources do not give it, so the caller must say what it is`

§ `Schedule 1: construction of certain references to relationships`

DECLARE `Reference to a relationship` IS ONE OF
    `a reference (however expressed) to any relationship between two persons`
    `a reference to a person whose father and mother were or were not married to, or civil partners of, each other at the time of his birth`
    `a reference cognate with a reference of the previous kind`
    `another reference`

-- src:344 | Construction of certain references to relationships
-- src:345 | In relation to England and Wales—
-- src:346 | (a) references (however expressed) to any relationship between two persons;
-- src:347 | (b) references to a person whose father and mother were or were not married to , or civil partners of, each other at the time of his birth; and
-- src:348 | (c) references cognate with references falling within paragraph (b) above,
-- src:349 | shall be construed in accordance with section 1 of the Family Law Reform Act 1987. [The date of the coming into force of that section]
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 1, relationships paragraph (src:344-349)
GIVEN reference IS A `Reference to a relationship`
      `in relation to England and Wales` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 construes the reference to a relationship in accordance with the Family Law Reform Act 1987` reference `in relation to England and Wales` MEANS
        `in relation to England and Wales`
    AND CONSIDER reference
        WHEN `a reference (however expressed) to any relationship between two persons` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a reference to a person whose father and mother were or were not married to, or civil partners of, each other at the time of his birth` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a reference cognate with a reference of the previous kind` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `another reference` THEN FALSE

§ `Schedule 1: construction of certain expressions relating to the police: Scotland`

DECLARE `Police reference` IS ONE OF
    `a police force`
    `a chief officer of police`
    `police authority`
    `the police area of the Police Service of Scotland`
    `a police force or police authority for any area`
    `a constable of, or appointed for, any area`
    `a chief constable of, or appointed for, any area`

-- src:350 | Construction of certain expressions relating to the police: Scotland
-- src:351 | In relation to Scotland—
-- src:352 | (a) references to a police force include references to the Police Service of Scotland;
-- src:353 | (b) references to a chief officer of police include references to the chief constable of the Police Service of Scotland;
-- src:354 | (c) “police authority” means the Scottish Police Authority;
-- src:355 | (d) the “police area” of the Police Service of Scotland is Scotland and references to a police force or police authority for any area include references to the Police Service of Scotland or, as the case may be, the Scottish Police Authority;
-- src:356 | (e) references to a constable or chief constable of, or appointed for, any area are to be construed as references to a constable or, as the case may be, the chief constable of, or appointed for, the Police Service of Scotland.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 1, police paragraph: Scotland (src:350-356)
GIVEN reference IS A `Police reference`
GIVETH A STRING
`Schedule 1 reads the police reference for Scotland` reference MEANS
    CONSIDER reference
    WHEN `a police force` THEN "the Police Service of Scotland"
    WHEN `a chief officer of police` THEN "the chief constable of the Police Service of Scotland"
    WHEN `police authority` THEN "the Scottish Police Authority"
    WHEN `the police area of the Police Service of Scotland` THEN "Scotland"
    WHEN `a police force or police authority for any area` THEN "the Police Service of Scotland or, as the case may be, the Scottish Police Authority"
    WHEN `a constable of, or appointed for, any area` THEN "a constable of, or appointed for, the Police Service of Scotland"
    WHEN `a chief constable of, or appointed for, any area` THEN "the chief constable of, or appointed for, the Police Service of Scotland"

§ `Schedule 2 para 4(5) and (6): "person" for offences, and the Water Act 1973`

-- src:422 | (5) The definition of “person”, so far as it includes bodies corporate, applies to any provision of an Act whenever passed relating to an offence punishable on indictment or on summary conviction.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 2 para 4(5) (src:422), with Sch 1 "Person" (src:298)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the provision relates to an offence punishable on indictment or on summary conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 2 para 4(5) applies the inclusion of bodies corporate in person to a provision of an Act passed on` day `the provision relates to an offence punishable on indictment or on summary conviction` `it is a body corporate` MEANS
    IF   `a Schedule 1 paragraph with the mark applies to the enactment` (`An enactment` WITH `its kind` IS `an Act`, `the day it was passed or made` IS day, `what it says about coming into force` IS `no provision`) (`a year is specified` 1889)
    THEN `Schedule 1 counts the body as a person` `it is a body corporate` FALSE
    ELSE `the provision relates to an offence punishable on indictment or on summary conviction` AND `it is a body corporate`

-- src:423 | (6) This paragraph applies to . . . the Water Act 1973 as if they were passed after 1st April 1974.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 2 para 4(6) (src:423)
GIVEN `it is the Water Act 1973` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 2 para 4(6) treats the Act as passed after 1st April 1974` `it is the Water Act 1973` MEANS
    `it is the Water Act 1973`

-- An Act "treated as passed after 1st April 1974" is passed on some day from 2 April 1974 on, and the paragraph does not say which. A year in the bracket bars it
-- only if the year is before 1974; a date in the bracket bars it only if the date is after 2 April 1974. Otherwise the mark does not decide.
-- src:413 | 4 (1) Subject to the following provisions of this paragraph—
-- src:414 | (a) paragraphs of Schedule 1 at the end of which a year or date . . . is specified or described apply, so far as applicable, to Acts passed on or after the date, or after the year, so specified or described: and
-- src:415 | (b) paragraphs of that Schedule at the end of which no year or date is specified or described apply, so far as applicable, to Acts passed at any time.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 2 para 4(6) (src:423), with para 4(1) (src:413-415)
GIVEN mark IS A `Mark at the end of a Schedule 1 paragraph`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 2 para 4(6) — a Schedule 1 paragraph with the mark applies to an Act treated as passed after 1st April 1974` mark MEANS
    CONSIDER mark
    WHEN `no year or date is specified` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a year is specified` y THEN
        IF   y LESS THAN 1974
        THEN TRUE
        ELSE `Schedule 2 para 4(6) treats the Act as passed after 1st April 1974 and names no day, so the mark of the paragraph is not decided`
    WHEN `a date is specified` d THEN
        IF   d AT MOST (YMD 1974 4 2)
        THEN TRUE
        ELSE `Schedule 2 para 4(6) treats the Act as passed after 1st April 1974 and names no day, so the mark of the paragraph is not decided`

§ `Schedule 2 para 5: definitions treated as included in Schedule 1`

DECLARE `Place that England may include` IS ONE OF
    `Berwick upon Tweed`
    `Monmouthshire`
    `Wales`
    `another place`

-- src:424 | 5 The following definitions shall be treated as included in Schedule 1 for the purposes specified in this paragraph—
-- src:425 | (a) in any Act passed before 1st April 1974, a reference to England includes Berwick upon Tweed and Monmouthshire and, in the case of an Act passed before the Welsh Language Act 1967, Wales;
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 2 para 5(a) (src:424-425)
GIVEN place IS A `Place that England may include`
      day IS A DATE
      `the day the Welsh Language Act 1967 was passed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 2 para 5(a) provides that a reference to England includes the place in an Act passed on` place day `the day the Welsh Language Act 1967 was passed` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `Berwick upon Tweed` THEN day LESS THAN (YMD 1974 4 1)
    WHEN `Monmouthshire` THEN day LESS THAN (YMD 1974 4 1)
    WHEN `Wales` THEN
        BRANCH
            IF day LESS THAN `the day the Welsh Language Act 1967 was passed` THEN TRUE
            IF day EQUALS `the day the Welsh Language Act 1967 was passed`
                THEN `Schedule 2 para 5(a) does not say whether an Act passed on the day the Welsh Language Act 1967 was passed was passed before it`
            OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHEN `another place` THEN FALSE

-- src:424 | 5 The following definitions shall be treated as included in Schedule 1 for the purposes specified in this paragraph—
-- src:426 | (b) in any Act passed before the commencement of this Act and after the year 1850, “land” includes messuages, tenements and hereditaments, houses and buildings of any tenure;
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 2 para 5(b) (src:424) and (src:426)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing that may be land`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 2 para 5(b) provides that land includes the thing in an Act passed on` thing day MEANS
        day LESS THAN `the day on which the Interpretation Act 1978 comes into force`
    AND DATE_YEAR day GREATER THAN 1850
    AND CONSIDER thing
        WHEN `a messuage` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a tenement or hereditament` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a house or building of any tenure` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Schedule 1's "Land" carries the mark [1st January 1979], so by Sch 2 para 4(1)(a) it reaches only an Act passed on or after that day; for an Act passed before it and
-- after the year 1850, para 5(b) gives the other list ("messuages, tenements and hereditaments, houses and buildings of any tenure"); for an earlier Act neither applies.
-- The two lists are never both in play for one Act.
-- src:276 | “Land” includes building and other structures, land covered with water, and any estate, interest, easement, servitude or right in or over land. [1st January 1979].
-- src:413 | 4 (1) Subject to the following provisions of this paragraph—
-- src:414 | (a) paragraphs of Schedule 1 at the end of which a year or date . . . is specified or described apply, so far as applicable, to Acts passed on or after the date, or after the year, so specified or described: and
-- src:415 | (b) paragraphs of that Schedule at the end of which no year or date is specified or described apply, so far as applicable, to Acts passed at any time.
-- src:424 | 5 The following definitions shall be treated as included in Schedule 1 for the purposes specified in this paragraph—
-- src:426 | (b) in any Act passed before the commencement of this Act and after the year 1850, “land” includes messuages, tenements and hereditaments, houses and buildings of any tenure;
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 1 "Land" (src:276), Sch 2 para 4(1) (src:413-415) and para 5(b) (src:424) and (src:426)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing that may be land`
      day   IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 and Schedule 2 para 5(b) — land includes the thing in an Act passed on` thing day MEANS
    IF   `a Schedule 1 paragraph with the mark applies to the enactment` (`An enactment` WITH `its kind` IS `an Act`, `the day it was passed or made` IS day, `what it says about coming into force` IS `no provision`) (`a date is specified` (YMD 1979 1 1))
    THEN `Schedule 1 counts the thing as land` thing
    ELSE `Schedule 2 para 5(b) provides that land includes the thing in an Act passed on` thing day

-- src:424 | 5 The following definitions shall be treated as included in Schedule 1 for the purposes specified in this paragraph—
-- src:427 | (c) in any Act passed before the commencement of the Criminal Procedure (Scotland) Act 1975, “the Summary Jurisdiction (Scotland) Acts” means Part II of that Act.
@ref Interpretation Act 1978 Sch 2 para 5(c) (src:424) and (src:427)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the day the Criminal Procedure (Scotland) Act 1975 came into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`Schedule 2 para 5(c) gives the meaning of the Summary Jurisdiction (Scotland) Acts in an Act passed on` day `the day the Criminal Procedure (Scotland) Act 1975 came into force` MEANS
    IF   day LESS THAN `the day the Criminal Procedure (Scotland) Act 1975 came into force`
    THEN JUST "Part II of that Act"
    ELSE NOTHING
